  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are the probabilities of a student passing three independent exams&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> respectively. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are the roots of equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the&nbsp;probability that the student passes in exactly one of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is"
